  "body": "## What changed\n\n- **Format (`crates/app/src/tool_library.rs`)**: a `.camtools` tool's `definition` may carry `body`, the same `ToolBodyDto` a `.camproj` tool stores (a drawn holder profile, a placed mesh, or a lathe holder). The key is additive: `camcraft-tools/1` stays, files without it read unchanged, and older builds ignore it. Export writes the body of every tool that has one. On read, a body is checked the way the project loader checks one: `ToolBodyDto::to_body` re-derives it and `tool_body::fits` must accept it. If either refuses, the whole file is refused and the tool is named. The clean-room note stays as it was.\n- **Command (`commands/tool_import.rs`)**: `ImportTools::with_holders(world, library, holders)` is still one undoable command. `ImportTools::new` is the same call with holders on. With holders on, each body is checked again at command creation. With holders off, every tool lands bare (holder cylinder only). The duplicate and rename rules are unchanged. The body counts toward \"identical\" only when one lands: a bare library tool matches the document's tool on its record alone, as before, and a tool that lands with a body must match the body too, otherwise it arrives as \"Name (2)\". `ImportReport` gains `holders` and `holders_left_out`, and both appear on the status line.\n- **UI (Tool library page)**: an \"Import tool holders\" checkbox next to Import library, ticked by default. It is passed to the command as its `holders` parameter and remembered per user in the prefs file (`importToolHolders`, written only when off), the same way as #877. It is not project state and not on the history.\n- **MCP**: `import_tool_library` takes an optional `holders` boolean (default true). The schema and description are updated, and the reply adds `holders` and `holders_left_out`. The script verb `cam.importTools(path)` keeps its arity (holders on).\n- **Process**: the `import_tool_library` line in the camcraft-mcp skill is updated, so `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` goes 16 -> 17. Other open process PRs also claim 17-20; whichever merges later takes the next number when it merges main.\n- Decision file: `docs/decisions/889-camtools-holder-body.md`.\n\n## How tested (local, macOS, debug, sccache; fork synced at v0.18.0)\n\nPinning tests:\n- `crates/app/tests/tool_library_holders.rs` (new, 5 tests):\n  - `export_import_with_holders_is_byte_stable` covers a drawn BT30 ER20 body and a mesh body; export -> import -> export gives identical bytes and the bodies are bit-identical.\n  - `holders_off_lands_every_tool_bare_and_undo_restores`\n  - `a_malformed_or_ill_fitting_body_refuses_the_file_by_name` covers a non-body, a bad outline, a mesh with no placement, and flutes running into the holder; nothing is applied and nothing goes on the history.\n  - `a_file_without_bodies_imports_as_before_and_the_skip_reads_bodies_only_when_one_lands`\n  - `mcp_import_tool_library_takes_the_holders_flag` covers the schema, off, the default on, the round trip over MCP, and refusal of a non-boolean.\n- `crates/app/tests/view_prefs.rs`: `the_tool_holder_import_choice_survives_a_restart`\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/tool_library_import.rs`: `the_toggle_stands_on_the_page_ticked_and_is_remembered_per_user` (AccessKit CheckBox role and toggled state, prefs written, not dirty) and `unticked_imports_bare_ticked_takes_the_holder_and_undo_restores`.\n\nSuites, all green:\n\n| Suite | Result |\n|---|---|\n| tool_library | 13 |\n| tool_library_holders | 5 |\n| view_prefs | 7 |\n| holder_library | 11 |\n| tool_body | 12 |\n| tool_body_bands | 13 |\n| tool_body_judged | 8 |\n| tool_body_view | 7 |\n| project_roundtrip | 71 |\n| mcp | 13 |\n| camcraft-ui lib, `--test-threads=1` | 533 passed, 5 ignored |\n\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean. No snapshot PNGs changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The real file dialog and click-through in a live window.\n- The holder count is shown after the import (status line and MCP reply), not before it, because the toggle stands on the page before any file is picked. The decision file explains this.\n- The drawn cutter outline (`ToolCutter`) and a holder-library entry name are not carried; see the decision file.\n\nChangelog: Tool library files (.camtools) carry each tool's holder body; the Tool library page's \"Import tool holders\" toggle (and MCP `import_tool_library` `holders`) chooses whether an import takes them (#889)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0\n\nFixes #889\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
